{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/memcached","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:07.822Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurelinux/base/memcached/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurelinux/base/memcached/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Memcached image for Azure Linux.\n\n### What is Azure Linux?\n\nAzure Linux is a Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. Azure Linux is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about Azure Linux, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Memcached?\n\nMemcached is an service that provides distributed hashmaps.\n\nSee: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memcached](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memcached)\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `1`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to Memcached version, Azure Linux build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running a `memcached` server locally\n\n`1.` Run the Azure Linux `memcached` container image with an exposed port for access.\n\n    docker run -d -p <host port>:11211 mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/memcached:1\n\nThe default container startup command is `memcached` with the user `memcache`. This launches `memcached` with the user `memcache`.\n\n### Launch Azure Linux shell\n\nThe Memcached image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to Launch Azure Linux shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/memcached:1 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nAzure Linux container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Azure Linux distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/azurelinux/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-12T02:11:16.4338667+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"28K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"1.6","digest":"sha256:03455f84d7be678a283a89df1a0d4062a879f8d2ac4a47f4cb81a9b14b2d3877","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:36:02.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1","digest":"sha256:03455f84d7be678a283a89df1a0d4062a879f8d2ac4a47f4cb81a9b14b2d3877","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:35:57.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1.6.27-6-azl3.0.20260909","digest":"sha256:03455f84d7be678a283a89df1a0d4062a879f8d2ac4a47f4cb81a9b14b2d3877","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:35:52.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1.6.27-6-azl3.0.20260909-arm64","digest":"sha256:224329a22fbbd81024c92d8d3102dee011cc850d8607d646ef90c3ad92511393","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:35:51.0000000+00:00",